      "binding": "specified",
      "variants": [
        {
          "id": "bank-sited",
          "status": "canonical",
          "note": "The house is set across a slope so the lower storey opens at grade on the downhill side and is buried on the uphill side, yielding a cool frost-free service level -- often over a spring -- with its own door, and a dry principal floor entered from the upper grade: 'two front doors on two different levels... the most reliable single tell of the tradition' (own long description, own diagnostic tell #4)."
        }
      ],
      "rule": "The ground is not levelled and dug into for a cellar in the English manner; it is built across, banking the service storey.",
